quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  60,6,"Indeed, there is an excellent example in them for you (to adopt) for whoever looks forward to Allah and the Last Day. But whoever turns away (should know that) Allah is the All-Sufficient, the All-Praiseworthy."
  60,7,"Allah may still bring about affection between you and those among them whom you (presently) hold as enemies. And Allah is All-Capable, and Allah is All-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  60,8,"Allah does not forbid you, regarding those who have not fought you on account of (your) religion, nor expelled you from your homes, from treating them kindly and being just towards them. Indeed, Allah loves those who are just."
  60,9,"Allah only forbids you to take those as allies who fought you because of (your) religion and expelled you from your homes or supported (others) in your expulsion. Whoever takes them as trusted friends (or allies), they are the wrongdoers."
  60,10,"O believers! When believing women come to you as emigrants, test their intentions. Allah knows best (the state of) their faith. Then, if you ascertain them to be faithful women, do not send them back to the disbelievers. These women are not lawful for those (idolators), nor are they lawful for them. And repay the disbelievers whatever (dowries) they have paid (to these believing women). There is no sin upon you in marrying them when you have given them their bridal gifts. Do not hold to the (marital) ties with disbelieving women. And demand (the disbelievers for repayment of) whatever you have spent (upon them as dowries), and let the disbelievers demand you for whatever they have spent. That is Allah’s judgement; He judges between you. And Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise."
  60,11,"If any of your wives deserts you, going over to the disbelievers, and later you acquire the spoils of war (from them), then pay those (idolators) whose wives have deserted them the equivalent of whatever (dowry) they had paid. And be God-conscious in Whom you are believers."
